= Navigation =

BITwiki navigation should support both deliberate study and exploratory traversal across a semantic knowledge graph.

== Navigation surfaces ==

=== Main Page ===
The public entry point and concise orientation surface.

=== Portals ===
High-level entry points into major knowledge fields. Historical Book Matter work described portals as '''intelligent entry points to recursive knowledge networks'''.

* [[Portal:Systems science]] — foundational/root orientation
* [[Portal:Science]]
* [[Portal:Biology]]
* [[Portal:Mathematics]]
* [[Portal:Philosophy]]
* [[Portal:Technology]]
* [[Portal:Electronics]]
* [[Portal:Energy]]
* [[Portal:Engineering]]
* [[Portal:Chemistry]]
* [[Portal:Physics]]
* [[Portal:Medicine]]

=== Indices ===
Large-scale maps and registries organized for lookup.

=== Outlines ===
Hierarchical decompositions used to understand the internal structure of a field without claiming the outline is the ontology itself.

=== Contents pages ===
Broad human-readable directories across major knowledge surfaces.

=== Categories ===
Human-readable classification and browsing groups.

=== Semantic queries and knowledge graphs ===
Computed/visual views over structured properties and relationships. Graphs are views over knowledge, not independent truth.

== Systems science orientation ==
Historical design placed Systems Science / Systems Theory as the top or root priority: individual knowledge domains are interpreted as interacting systems rather than isolated silos. This is an intellectual orientation, not a demand that every page literally be nested beneath one category.

